      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>This is a free <strong>nursery self-evaluation template</strong> for a Scottish early learning and childcare setting. It is structured around the key questions of the Care Inspectorate's quality framework How good is our early learning and childcare?, so the judgements you make here map to what an inspector assesses. Copy it into your own document, print it, or run it as a live workflow. The template is deliberately simple: for each key question you record the evidence you can see, grade yourself on the six-point scale, and write the action that would move the grade.</p><p>In Scotland, early learning and childcare is regulated by the Care Inspectorate, not Ofsted, which covers England only, and not CQC. The exact quality indicator wording changes from time to time, so always work from the current published framework and the Health and Social Care Standards. Treat this as general information, not regulatory advice.</p>"
    },
