  "seoBody": "<h2>A free nursery self-evaluation template for Scotland</h2><p>In Scotland, early learning and childcare is regulated by the Care Inspectorate. Ofsted regulates childcare in England; in Scotland it is the Care Inspectorate, and it is not CQC either. Nurseries self-evaluate and are inspected against the Health and Social Care Standards and the Care Inspectorate's quality framework How good is our early learning and childcare?, graded on a six-point scale from unsatisfactory to excellent.</p><p>This page is a free, printable template structured around that framework's key questions: care, play and learning; the setting; the staff team including ratios and safeguarding; and leadership. For each quality indicator area it gives you the evidence to gather, a self-grade column on the six-point scale, and an improvement action to fill in. Copy it into your own document, print it and take it round the setting, or run it as a live workflow. The exact indicator wording is set by How good is our early learning and childcare?, so always work from the current published version and the Health and Social Care Standards.</p><h2>How to use the template</h2><p>Take each key question in turn. Walk the nursery, note the evidence you can actually see against each row, grade yourself honestly, and write the one action that would move the grade. The value is not the grade you award yourself; it is the gap you find while there is still time to close it. When every row has an honest grade, take each row graded three or below and turn its improvement action into a task with an owner and a date. That is the live improvement plan an inspector wants to see.</p><h2>What Quickler captures, and where it stops</h2><p>Quickler can run this same template as a WhatsApp workflow. The manager or room lead walks the nursery and answers each prompt with text, a voice note or a photo, and the report and improvement plan build themselves. Each low self-grade becomes a flagged action automatically.</p><p>The honest boundary: Quickler is an audit and self-evaluation and evidence tool. It is not a children's records system, a learning journal, an attendance register or a child protection case-management system, and it holds no child's personal data. For safeguarding it records that a check was done and captures the evidence, without copying any child's personal information. The child protection record stays in your setting's own system as the single source of truth. Quickler is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Care Inspectorate, and whether your evidence satisfies an inspection is a judgement for you and your inspector. Treat this page as general information, not regulatory advice.</p><h2>Pricing</h2><p>Pricing is only for active users: [[price:bundles]]. An active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, with a £20 minimum, and dormant users are free. There is a free tier of 20 reports a month and up to 10 photos per report, no card and no trial clock, so a nursery can run its first self-evaluation without committing.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/nursery-self-evaluation-scotland.html\">Nursery self-evaluation Scotland guide</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-inspectorate-self-evaluation-template-scotland.html\">Care Inspectorate self-evaluation template</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/childminder-self-evaluation-scotland.html\">Childminder self-evaluation Scotland</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/nursery-self-evaluation-england.html\">Nursery self-evaluation England</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/guides.html\">All guides</a></li></ul>",
